{"id":"sh/nm9sfmtw","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":71,"width":710,"height":100},"text":"Perigee","style":{"fontSize":84,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/sjmtkbal","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":181,"width":1130,"height":60},"text":"Investigate change in NASA’s infrared sky","style":{"fontSize":40,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/tkvutgr6","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":262,"width":1136,"height":82},"text":"A free web app for students, teachers and astronomy clubs to compare observations from NASA’s SPHEREx infrared telescope and explain what the evidence supports.","style":{"fontSize":29,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/1wzy9wnm","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":381,"width":553,"height":37},"text":"The problem","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/0vqx0r61","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":426,"width":553,"height":176},"text":"Two images of the same sky can look different because a star moved, the telescope sampled another infrared wavelength, or a pixel is unreliable. Seeing a change is only the start; the observer needs a way to decide what caused it.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/zuhg7m5g","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":381,"width":561,"height":37},"text":"What we built","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/etofyhob","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":426,"width":561,"height":176},"text":"Perigee combines aligned images, guided comparison checks and a saved evidence notebook. A learner finishes with their own explanation, the observations behind it and links back to NASA’s archive. Three cases teach the process; five targets and live search extend it.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/90zydwny","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":607,"width":1184,"height":28},"text":"Team Perigee, Planet X and SPHEREx challenge","style":{"fontSize":21,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ozqx4r6d","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":645,"width":1184,"height":25},"text":"Sathvik Loke, Sagar Raut, Akshobya Rao, Aditya Raut, Suhrit Bestavemula and Neeraj Movva","style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0}
